        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "No human right is more basic than freedom of speech, which ensures individual expression and guarantees the open flow of ideas in society. It arose as a pillar of modern political thought during the late eighteenth century, and in 1948, it was recognized by the United Nations as a universal right. It protects not only",
